      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2010 National Kidney Foundation, Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Transient episodes of pain are common in autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease (ADPKD). A small fraction of patients have disabling chronic pain. In this review, we discuss the etiologies of pain in ADPKD; review how ADPKD patients should be assessed; and discuss medical, surgical, and other management options."
      },
